      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "The original idea was came from:\n\nhttps://feedback.vrchat.com/localization/p/buttons-and-titles-in-wings-overflow-with-long-strings\n\nSeparate translation of UI and tooltips:\n\nhttps://feedback.vrchat.com/localization/p/select-tooltips-language-can-be-keep-saved-in-live-version-and-being-a-sub-setti",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2024-01-31T10:00:55.525Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Though translation, some simple concepts will become more verbose. This will cause UI text fields to overflow, hiding some of it's content. This will happen with narrow menu interfaces, like the \"Wing Menu.\"\n\nRecently, we suggested that there should be separate settings for UI and tooltip localization, allowing the use of translated tooltips to be used along with English UI. For a fully translated interface, we suggest the use of UI animation to avoid overflowing text.\n\nWe have two suggestions. Both normally keep text in a single line, and use UI animation to reveal the full content.\n\n- Firstly, we suggest the use of auto-scrolling. Normally, UI elements would show an initial span of text. Then, while the pointer is hovering, the remainder of the text would scroll into view.\n\n- Secondly, we suggest the use of resizing UI elements. Again, normally, UI elements would show an initial span of text. Then, while the pointer is hovering, the UI element would expand it's height to show the full text.\n\nAdditionally, I recommend against resizing the text itself. Doing so would result in difficult to read text. Especially for some low-PPD VR headsets, such as the VIVE PRO.",
